Update the properties of a security group.

USAGE:
  scw instance security-group update [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  security-group-id           ID of the security group to update
  [name]                      New name for the security group
  [description]               New description for the security group
  [disable-default-rules]     Whether to disable default rules
  [tags.{index}]              New tags for the security group
  [project-default]           Whether this should be the default security group for the project
  [inbound-default-action]    New default action for inbound rules (unknown_action | accept | drop)
  [outbound-default-action]   New default action for outbound rules (unknown_action | accept | drop)
  [stateless]                 Whether the security group should be stateless
  [zone=fr-par-1]             Zone to target. If none is passed will use default zone from the config (fr-par-1 | fr-par-2 | fr-par-3 | nl-ams-1 | nl-ams-2 | nl-ams-3 | pl-waw-1 | pl-waw-2 | pl-waw-3 | it-mil-1)

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for update
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta             Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
      --web              open console page for the current resource
